    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1930" root="بد" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِدٌّ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُدٌّ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَدِيدٌ</span></b>  (T, K) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَدِيدَةٌ</span></b> , (K,) <i>A like; a fellow; an equal.</i> (T,
K.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ بِدُّهُ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَدِيدُهُ</span></b>  <i>He,</i> or <i>it, is
the like, &amp;c., of him,</i> or <i>it.</i> (T.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُمَ بِدَّانِ</span>
<i>They two are likes,</i> or <i>fellows,</i> or <i>equals.</i> (TA.)
And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَتُكَلِّمَنِى</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَنْتَ لِى بِبَدِيدٍ</span></b>  <i>Thou art not
my like,</i> or <i>fellow,</i> or <i>equal, that thou shouldst
speak to me.</i> (TA.)

